+        the first would silently keep whatever `_uuid` the first call's
+        `__init__` happened to draw, forever -- not reproducible per seed,
+        just frozen. Redrawing on every `reset()` (which every
+        `build_client`/`boot_from_save` call makes, after `seed_ids`) is
+        what actually ties `_uuid` to the build's seed.
+        """
+        self._uuid = new_id()
         if reset_client:
             self._client = None
         if reset_world:
